Lab 7: Handling Errors and Exceptions in Camel
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Implement comprehensive error handling mechanisms in Apache Camel routes
Configure retry policies for transient failures
Set up and configure Dead Letter Channels (DLQ) for failed messages
Test various error scenarios to validate error recovery behavior
Interpret Camel logs and output files to confirm correct error recovery behavior
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Apache Camel concepts and routing
Familiarity with Java programming and Maven
Understanding of exception handling in Java
Basic Linux command line operations
Required Software
This lab assumes a Linux-based practice environment (a personal VM, container, or Al Nafi cloud machine) with the following installed:

java -version
mvn -version
If Java 11+ and Maven 3.8+ are not present, install them with your distribution's package manager, for example:

sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y openjdk-11-jdk maven
All other dependencies (Apache Camel 3.20.x, SLF4J) are declared in the Maven pom.xml created in Task 1 and will be downloaded automatically by Maven.

