Expected result: Output shows Tests run: 4, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 and BUILD SUCCESS. This confirms, in isolation, that normal messages succeed, business errors skip retries, technical errors retry until exhaustion and land in the DLQ, and transient failures recover before exhaustion.

Task 3: Run the Application and Analyze Dead Letter Behavior
Subtask 3.1: Start the Application
Run the application in the foreground so you can observe log output directly. This will process the four files placed in input/ during Task 2.

timeout 30 mvn exec:java -Dexec.mainClass="com.example.camel.ErrorHandlingApplication"
The timeout 30 wrapper stops the process automatically after 30 seconds, which is enough time for the file poller (delay=2000) to pick up all four files and for retries (redelivery delay up to 8 seconds, 3 retries) to complete.

Deliverable: The command runs to completion without a Java stack trace escaping the application (Camel-caught exceptions inside routes are expected and will appear as ERROR log lines, which is correct behavior, not a crash).

